{title: After the Rain}
{artist: Freevia Demo}
{composer: Freevia Demo}
{lyricist: Freevia Demo}
{key: Am}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 6/8}
{comment: Original demonstration lyrics and illustrative chord chart created for Freevia; no recording or synced timing supplied.}

{start_of_intro}
[Am] [F] [C] [E7]
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Am]Rain on the window is [F]losing its voice,
[C]Clouds in the valley are [E7]making a choice.
[Am]Stay with the silence a [F]moment or two,
[C]Somewhere the hillside is [E7]coming in view.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]After the [C]rain, we can [G]walk out a[Am]gain,
[F]Follow the [C]river a[E7]round the next [Am]bend.
[F]Nothing is [C]lost that can [G]find us a[Am]gain,
[Dm]Seeds in the [Am]earth will a[E7]wake after [Am]rain.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Am]Water is shining on [F]every green leaf,
[C]Air has the scent of a [E7]quiet relief.
[Am]Take what is heavy and [F]set it aside,
[C]There is a path on the [E7]farther hillside.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]After the [C]rain, we can [G]walk out a[Am]gain,
[F]Follow the [C]river a[E7]round the next [Am]bend.
[F]Nothing is [C]lost that can [G]find us a[Am]gain,
[Dm]Seeds in the [Am]earth will a[E7]wake after [Am]rain.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[Dm]Let the last [Am]thunder fade,
[F]See the room the [C]storm has made.
[Dm]In the space be[Am]tween the trees,
[F]We can hear the [E7]evening breeze.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus}
[F]After the [C]rain, we can [G]walk out a[Am]gain,
[F]Follow the [C]river a[E7]round the next [Am]bend.
[F]Nothing is [C]lost that can [G]find us a[Am]gain,
[Dm]Seeds in the [Am]earth will a[E7]wake after [Am]rain.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_outro}
[Dm]Take one more [Am]step down the [E7]lane,
[F]Home is a[C]wake after [Am]rain.
{end_of_outro}
